  "question": {
    "text": "A generator has armature resistance of $0.1 \\Omega$ and develops an induced emf of $120 \\mathrm{~V}$ when driven at its rated speed. Its terminal voltage when a current of $50 \\mathrm{~A}$ is being drawn is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "zbZFk",
      "text": "\n$120 \\mathrm{~V}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3l3uD",
      "text": "\n$5 \\mathrm{~V}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "j0m1K",
      "text": "\n$115 \\mathrm{~V}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "CjuVB",
      "text": "\n$70 \\mathrm{~V}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Armature resistance $R=0.1 \\Omega$\nInduced emf, $e=120 \\mathrm{~V}$\nCurrent drown, $I=50 \\mathrm{~A}$\nWe know that,\n$e=V+I R$\nor, $V=e-I R=120-50 \\times 0.1=115 \\mathrm{~V}$",
    "image": null
  },
